Write two unit test files for the tutors-apps project.

## File 1: `tests/unit/services/schemas/schemas.test.ts`

Validate that Zod schemas from `tests/contracts/schemas.ts` correctly accept valid data and reject invalid data. This ensures the contracts stay in sync with actual domain types.

Test the following schemas with valid/invalid cases:

**TutorsIdSchema** — valid: `{ name: "A", login: "a", email: "a@b.com", image: "http://x.png", share: "true", sentiment: "neutral" }`. Invalid: missing `login` field.

**CourseVisitSchema** — valid: `{ id: "c1", title: "Course", lastVisit: new Date(), credits: "Author" }`. Invalid: missing `id`.

**LoUserSchema** — valid: `{ fullName: "A", avatar: "http://x.png", id: "u1", sentiment: "neutral" }`. Invalid: missing `id`.

**LoRecordSchema** — valid: full LoRecord with user. Invalid: missing `courseId`.

**CourseSentimentIdSchema** — valid: each of "neutral", "fine", "delighted", "confident", "overwhelmed", "confused", "drained". Invalid: "happy" (not in enum).

**LayoutTypeSchema** — valid: "expanded", "compacted". Invalid: "wide".

**CardStyleTypeSchema** — valid: "portrait", "landscape", "circular". Invalid: "square".

**CourseUrlResultSchema** — valid: `{ courseId: "x", courseUrl: "x.netlify.app" }`. Invalid: missing courseUrl.

**CourseSchema** — valid: minimal course object. Invalid: missing title.

Use `assertValid` and `isValid` from `tests/contracts/validators.ts` to test. Import schemas from `tests/contracts/schemas.ts`.

Use `describe` per schema, `it` per case, vitest globals.

## File 2: `tests/unit/services/community/presence-service.test.ts`

Test the `refreshLoRecord` function exported from `src/lib/services/community/services/presence.svelte.ts` at line 100.

This is a pure function:
```typescript
export function refreshLoRecord(loEvent: LoRecord, nextLoEvent: LoRecord) {
  loEvent.loRoute = `https://tutors.dev${nextLoEvent.loRoute}`;
  loEvent.title = nextLoEvent.title;
  loEvent.type = nextLoEvent.type;
  loEvent.user = nextLoEvent.user;
  if (nextLoEvent.icon) {
    loEvent.icon = nextLoEvent.icon;
    loEvent.img = undefined;
  } else {
    loEvent.img = nextLoEvent.img;
    loEvent.icon = undefined;
  }
}
```

IMPORTANT: This file (`presence.svelte.ts`) imports from `partysocket` and `$env/static/public` at module level. The vitest config already aliases `$env/static/public` to the mock. For partysocket, you need to mock it:
```typescript
vi.mock("partysocket", () => {
  return { default: vi.fn() };
});
```

Also mock `$lib/services/community/utils/supabase-client` since it's imported by presence.svelte.ts:
```typescript
vi.mock("$lib/services/community/utils/supabase-client", () => ({
  upsertTutorsConnectLatestLo: vi.fn(),
  supabase: {}
}));
```

Test cases for refreshLoRecord:
1. Updates loRoute with tutors.dev prefix
2. Updates title, type, user
3. When nextLoEvent has icon: sets icon, clears img
4. When nextLoEvent has no icon: sets img, clears icon
5. Validate with LoRecordSchema after mutation

Use `createLoRecord` from `tests/fixtures/lo-factory.ts` to create test data.
